Contents\par
--------\par
I.\tab Obtaining Minor Updates\par
II. \tab Network installations\par
III. \tab New features/bug fixes\par
IV. \tab Attention Canon Bubblejet Printer Owners.\par
V. \tab Attention HP Laserjet series 5 Printer Owners.\par
======================================================\par
\par
\par
I.  OBTAINING MINOR UPDATES\par
Minor updates to FIRE are currently available on our World Wide Web site at:  \par
\tab\par
\tab http://www.elitesoft.com\par
\par
\par
II. NETWORK INSTALLATIONS:\par
\par
The FIRE program is not specifically designed to run on a network.  It is only intended to be run on the same computer on which it was installed.  However various program directories can be located on a network.  This procedure enables the setting of these directories immediately prior to program installation.\par
\par
If you want to install FIRE with different than default directories, open a command prompt and type:\par
\par
\tab [your floppy drive name]:SETUP /M\par
\par
to install FIRE.  This will enable you to specify the locations of your WINDOWS, SYSTEM and TEMP directories.\par
\par
\par
III. NEW FEATURES/BUG FIXES:\par
\par
Version 6.0.244 12/22/10\par
1. Fixed an error on the General Project Data report that occurred with metric projects.\par
\par
Version 6.0.243 11/17/10\par
1. Added an option to print a fitting legend on the Pipe Input and Pipe Output reports.\par
\par
Version 6.0.242 10/21/10\par
1. Modified the file handling features (such as opening or closing or saving a project) so that they conform with new company standards.\par
\par
Version 6.0.241 9/21/10\par
1. Made pipe sorting faster on the Edit Pipe Data window.\par
\par
2. Made scrolling and data modification faster on the Edit Node Data window.\par
\par
3. Fixed a problem with the Overall Pipe Output Data report.  The water velocity and a few other pipe characteristics were not being printed on this report for some projects.\par
\par
Version 6.0.239 7/22/10\par
1. Changed the way the program handles some calculations. If the initial damping factor is less than 99 and divergence occurs during calculations, the calculations will be restarted automatically using an initial damping factor of 99.\par
\par
Version 6.0.238 6/21/10\par
1. Fixed a problem that prevented calculations from finishing when a large number of inactive pipes was present in a valid pipe network.\par
\par
2. Clarified the warning message that appears when divergence occurs during calculations.\par
\par
3. Changed the way the program handles some calculations.  If residual pressure estimates are used and divergence occurs during calculations, the calculations will be restarted automatically without using residual pressure estimates.\par
\par
Version 6.0.237 4/26/10\par
1. Made it so if Supply mode is selected, the automatic peaking check box is unchecked and grayed out.\par
\par
2. Fixed a problem that made the program crash when a new metric project was started and the Edit Pipe Data window was opened.\par
\par
Version 6.0.236 4/8/10\par
1. Fixed a problem with the metric conversion of the pipe friction loss per foot.\par
\par
2. Made it so the supply pressure at the inflow node can have two decimal places.\par
\par
Version 6.0.235 3/18/10\par
1. In the Node Input Data report added information used in combined K-factor calculations for sprinklers on branch lines.\par
\par
2. In the Overall Pipe Output Data report added the q value (added flow) of each pipe and replaced velocity pressure with total pressure.\par
\par
Version 6.0.234 2/3/10\par
1. Made it so Fire links with AutoCAD MEP 2010.\par
\par
Version 6.0.233 1/22/10\par
1. Fixed a problem with the Auto Save feature.\par
