Version 6.0.223 2/13/09\par
1. Fixed a problem that caused the pipe lengths and elevations to be incorrect when an AutoCAD MEP drawing with drawing units set to millimeters was imported into Fire.\par
\par
Version 6.0.222 12/19/08\par
1. Fixed a data loss problem.  When you click the Open Selected Project button in the Exploring window while a modified project is open, you will now be asked if you want to save the open project.\par
\par
2. Fixed a problem that caused a certain pipe section to be printed multiple times on the Pipe Input Data report.\par
\par
3. Made it so Fire will not calculate results when all K-Factors are zero and the project is in Demand mode.\par
\par
4. Made it so high water velocity warnings for non-autosized pipes can be turned off without erasing any autosizing constraints.\par
